Feature: Calculate actual sales value per brand, country, territory, year, and month

  This feature calculates the actual_value for each combination of brand_name, country_code, territory_id, year, and month by summing sales_value from purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales and sales_net_price_local from purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales. Only records where source_system_name in both tables exists in purgo_playground.control_table.source_system are included.

  Background:
    Given the following tables exist in the purgo_playground schema:
      | t3_itm_territory_sales |
      | t3_ttm_territory_sales |
      | control_table          |
    And t3_itm_territory_sales has columns: country_code, brand_name, source_system_name, territory_id, sales_value (double), sales_month (date)
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales has columns: country_code, brand_name, source_system_name, territory_id, sales_net_price_local (double), fiscal_date (date)
    And control_table has columns: country_code, source_system, brand_name

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value for valid brand/country/territory/month/year combinations (happy path)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
      | <cc>         | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.0 | 200.0 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 300.0 |
      | DE   | BRANDY    | IQVIA     | IQVIA     | T002  | 50.0  | 75.0  | 2022-12-01 | 2022-12-20 | 2022 | 12 | 125.0 |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude records where source_system_name does not exist in control_table (error path)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set does not contain a row for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | fd         | y    | m  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | IQVIA     | T001  | 100.0 | 200.0 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | DE   | BRANDY    | IQVIA     | SAP       | T002  | 50.0  | 75.0  | 2022-12-01 | 2022-12-20 | 2022 | 12 |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude records where source_system_name exists in control_table but for a different brand_name or country_code (error path)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | OTHERBRAND |
      | XX           | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set does not contain a row for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | fd         | y    | m  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.0 | 200.0 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |

  Scenario Outline: Handle null sales_value or sales_net_price_local as zero in calculation (validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
      | <cc>         | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1    | sv2    | sm         | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | null   | 200.0  | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 200.0 |
      | DE   | BRANDY    | IQVIA     | IQVIA     | T002  | 50.0   | null   | 2022-12-01 | 2022-12-20 | 2022 | 12 | 50.0  |
      | FR   | BRANDZ    | SAP       | SAP       | T003  | null   | null   | 2021-01-01 | 2021-01-10 | 2021 | 1  | 0.0   |

  Scenario Outline: Validate year and month extraction from date columns (validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
      | <cc>         | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.0 | 200.0 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 300.0 |
      | DE   | BRANDY    | IQVIA     | IQVIA     | T002  | 50.0  | 75.0  | 2022-12-31 | 2022-12-01 | 2022 | 12 | 125.0 |

  Scenario: Exclude records where either t3_itm_territory_sales or t3_ttm_territory_sales is missing for a combination (inner join enforcement)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | US           | BRANDX     | SAP               | T001         | 100.0       | 2023-05-01   |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | DE           | BRANDY     | IQVIA             | T002         | 75.0                  | 2022-12-20   |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | US           | SAP           | BRANDX     |
      | DE           | IQVIA         | BRANDY     |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set does not contain a row for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | US           | BRANDX     | T001         | 2023 | 5     |
      | DE           | BRANDY     | T002         | 2022 | 12    |

  Scenario Outline: Validate aggregation when multiple records exist for the same group (aggregation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1a>      | <sm>         |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1b>      | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2a>                | <fd>         |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2b>                | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
      | <cc>         | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1a  | sv1b  | sv2a  | sv2b  | sm         | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.0 | 50.0  | 200.0 | 25.0  | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 375.0 |

  Scenario Outline: Validate output data types and formats (output validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <sv2>                 | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | <cc>         | <ssn1>        | <bn>       |
      | <cc>         | <ssn2>        | <bn>       |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set contains columns with the following data types:
      | column        | data_type |
      | country_code  | string    |
      | brand_name    | string    |
      | territory_id  | string    |
      | year          | int       |
      | month         | int       |
      | actual_value  | double    |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | fd         |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.0 | 200.0 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 |

  Scenario: Validate error message when required columns are missing (schema validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales is missing the column sales_value
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then an error is raised with message "Column 'sales_value' does not exist in table 't3_itm_territory_sales'"

  Scenario: Validate error message when date columns are not in date format (schema validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales.sales_month is of type string instead of date
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then an error is raised with message "Column 'sales_month' must be of type DATE"

  Scenario: Validate exclusion of records with null brand_name, country_code, or territory_id (validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | null         | BRANDX     | SAP               | T001         | 100.0       | 2023-05-01   |
      | US           | null       | SAP               | T001         | 100.0       | 2023-05-01   |
      | US           | BRANDX     | SAP               | null         | 100.0       | 2023-05-01   |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | US           | BRANDX     | SAP               | T001         | 200.0                 | 2023-05-15   |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | US           | SAP           | BRANDX     |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set does not contain any row with null in country_code, brand_name, or territory_id

  Scenario: Validate that only records with matching year and month in both tables are included (join validation)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | US           | BRANDX     | SAP               | T001         | 100.0       | 2023-05-01   |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | US           | BRANDX     | SAP               | T001         | 200.0                 | 2023-06-01   |
    And control_table contains:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
      | US           | SAP           | BRANDX     |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result set does not contain a row for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | US           | BRANDX     | T001         | 2023 | 5     |
      | US           | BRANDX     | T001         | 2023 | 6     |
